Define or give the reference of the follow up and corrective action procedure.
This procedure must be able to handle internal (ATO CMS findings) and external findings (any findings made by a third party).
This procedure must address the following:
Identification of corrective action;
Person responsible for rectification;
Feedback system to the accountable manager providing an independent assessment of corrective action, implementation and completion;
Monitoring of corrective action programme;
Ensuring that the corrective action contain the necessary elements;
Evaluation of the effectiveness of the corrective action programme;
Reporting of significant non-compliances to the competent authority.

